# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. Both come from the upstream Python template, where
# they cover a virtualenv created in place (`virtualenv .` puts `lib/` and `lib64/` next to
# `bin/`). A bare `lib/` matches at any depth and would swallow the source folders that
# SvelteKit (`$lib`), Astro, Vue, Nuxt, Next.js, Remix and Angular all keep at `src/lib` or
# `app/lib`. Re-including those with `!` would be worse, because a negation also overrides
# every earlier rule, which would drag `node_modules`, `dist` and `.DS_Store` back in with
# them. A venv in its own directory stays ignored through `.venv`, `venv/`, `env/` and
# `ENV/`. A venv at any other nested path needs a per-repo rule.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
